<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Autonomist Party (Fiume)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1896</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Autonomist Party was a political party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rijeka">Fiume</a>, now Rijeka, founded in 1896, which defended the city's self-government against Hungarian centralism and later against annexation by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>. Led after 1918 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riccardo-zanella">Riccardo Zanella</a>, it won the elections of April 1921 in the Free State of Fiume, but its government was overthrown by Fascists in March 1922.</p></div>
